      "stageRecord": "The silent subject DP moves from Spec-VP to Spec-IP, leaving an A-trace in its Experiencer position. Finite I licenses nominative Case on the resulting subject chain through the Spec–head relation. Portuguese null-subject licensing allows pro to remain unpronounced, and the first-person singular agreement identifies its referent as the speaker. The object clitic is a nonreflexive pronoun: its argument chain must be locally free under Principle B and is not bound by the first-person subject. Its referent may be an appropriate masculine entity or a contextually supplied neutral referent; that interpretive difference does not require a different syntactic derivation. The completed root IP represents the unmarked declarative without positing an additional CP layer. Its pronounced terminals, in order, are exactly Vi, o, ontem, yielding the interpretation 'I saw him/it yesterday.'",
